,title,link,text,language,family
0,Haisla people - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haisla_people,"The Haisla (Haisla: x̄áʼisla, lit. 'dwellers downriver') are a First Nation who reside in Kitamaat. [2] The Haisla consist of two bands: the Kitamaat people, residing in upper Douglas Channel and Devastation Channel, and the Kitlope People, inhabiting upper Princess Royal Channel and Gardner Canal in British Columbia, Canada.",Haisla,Wakashan
1,Haisla language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haisla_language,"Haisla (Haisla: X̄aʼislak̓ala / X̌àh̓isl̩ak̓ala, [ˈχaʔislakʼala]) is a First Nations Wakashan language spoken by the Haisla people of the North Coast region of the Canadian province of British Columbia, who are based in the village of Kitamaat.",Haisla,Wakashan
2,The Haisla Nation & People: Wakashan - YouTube,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2H5sryTw62c,"This is a video for the: ""The Haisla Nation & People"", a northern Wakashan speaking People whose main settlement is located in Kitamaat Village, B.C., on ""Turtle Island"". There are also over 2300 ...",Haisla,Wakashan
3,"Stream Haisla Nation music | Listen to songs, albums, playlists for ...",https://soundcloud.com/haisla-nation,"Play Haisla Nation and discover followers on SoundCloud | Stream tracks, albums, playlists on desktop and mobile.",Haisla,Wakashan
4,Haisla History - Haisla Nation,https://haisla.ca/haisla-history/,"Haisla History Since Time Immemorial The x̄á'isla, also known as the Haisla, are the Indigenous people of Kitamaat Village and the surrounding lands and waters of the Kitimat region in British Columbia. Since time immemorial, the x̄á'isla have lived on their unceded territory, sustaining themselves through fishing, hunting, and trade.",Haisla,Wakashan
5,case study | Haisla First Nation - xpan interactive,https://xpan.ca/case-study-haisla-first-nation/,"Storytelling is a pillar of the Haisla culture, and the Haisla Nation Council (HNC) saw an opportunity to share culturally significant stories of traditions, celebrations, and events in the community through a series of short videos. In addition to helping in the preservation of language, music, and , traditions, digital assets such as video and other media can be shared with band members and ...",Haisla,Wakashan
6,Haisla Nation,https://haisla.ca/,"The Haisla Nation Organization is the band government of the Haisla people. Our mission is to build a powerful, prosperous and proud community, healthy in mind, body and spirit.",Haisla,Wakashan
7,Haisla Braid Singers & Dancers - Facebook,https://www.facebook.com/groups/317329106252868/,"Haisla Braid Singers & Dancers, is a group of Singers, Drummers & Dancers. Our Culture is our Passion, our Medicine and it is our goal to keep the songs sung, the dances danced, for our future Singers, Drummers & Dancers.",Haisla,Wakashan
8,Haisla Nation - YouTube,https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLZV9hUnphuOMxmHWbXQ8tyUlluA1jpoUf,"Share your videos with friends, family, and the world",Haisla,Wakashan
9,x̄á'isla LanguageCloud,https://haisla.languagecloud.ca/home/sounds,"Users of this site must come with respect for the Language, Culture, and Land of the Haisla Nation. We expect all users to honor and respect the traditions, values, and rights of the Haisla Nation.",Haisla,Wakashan
